// REFUTATION PIN (silent-class-inventory D641/D681). A byte copy of
// `tests/cases/functions/structural-generic.vl`, carried here so the SEVEN-SECOND gate
// holds the price of D641's refused widening rather than only `deno task test`.
//
// The refused candidate resolves an un-annotated generic struct return by matching the
// shape's PRINTED SPELLING (`structIndexOfTypeName`). `addx` below instantiates at i32 and
// at f64; both instances re-check to `{x: <error>}` (an un-pinnable parameter binds to
// `TY_ERR`), both print the same text, both match the i32 row, and this module goes from
// `runs` to check-clean invalid wasm (`expected i32, found f64`). Re-measured 2026-08-31:
// it still does. D681's shipped resolver is NOMINAL (`sTyIx[si] == ty`) and cannot collide
// this way — this cell is what keeps that distinction honest.
// @run
// @log 4
// @log 6
// @log 3
// @log 4
// Fully-inferred structural generics (ROADMAP A13): an operator on an inference
// hole (`self.x + b.x`) no longer errors — the operands are concretized per call
// site (monomorphization), and codegen reads the concrete type from the instance
// scope (`codegenType`). `add` works on `{x, y}`; `addx` instantiates at both i32
// and f64 from its two call sites.
function add(self, b) { x: self.x + b.x, y: self.y + b.y }
const r = add({x: 1, y: 2}, {x: 3, y: 4})
print(r.x)
print(r.y)
function addx(self, b) { x: self.x + b.x }
const p = addx({x: 1}, {x: 2})
print(p.x)
const q = addx({x: 1.5}, {x: 2.5})
print(q.x)
